From 1ec0dcce5fc40e1ab35a407ec4fc7988733b858c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 06:37:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban chat waits: continue asks too, the answer
 wakes the card, reachable chats only

Second review and adversarial pass of #3647:
- kanban_continue recorded the chat wait but posted no decision_requested
  (the incident again under a new label). It posts it now.
- A chat wait with no probe (clock_only) slept to its clock although the
  notice says the answering comment wakes it. park_probe gives every chat
  wait a `wait-comment --after-id <newest comment>` probe (the park's own
  comment is older, so it never fires it); the park is then not clock-only.
- has_chat_subscriber counted tui rows whose chat the sweeper drops (archived,
  moved, worker transcript, deleted) and hub rows in notify+wake mode (legacy
  backfill). Now: never hub; tui only when tui_chat_reachable (same rules as
  tui_gateway.notice_fanout, read-only; an orphan-reaped Desktop chat stays
  reachable, as the live orchestrator was); messaging rows only in wake modes.
- Tighter ORCHESTRATOR_WAIT: qualified orchestrator/chat nouns or the
  orchestrator's decision words; citations and negations ("per the
  orchestrator's decision", "no orchestrator decision") and product names
  ("Airflow orchestrator release") do not match; adds "orchestrator to
  decide", "creator chat's answer", "origin session's call".

Tests: continue and CLI block --kind time with the live payload; a clock-only
chat wait gets the probe, which ignores the park comment and fires on the
answer (wait-comment CLI); archived/moved/worker/kanban-source/missing chats
and a hub notify+wake row are refused; an orphan-reaped Desktop chat counts;
12 matcher cases. 16 of 42 fail on the previous head; 33 neighbouring files,
571 tests pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
